+### Transferring a user to another organization
+
+`POST /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` with `{"toOrgId":"globex"}` moves a user (for
+example between group companies). Rules:
+
+- The caller must be an org admin of `{orgID}`. Callers from another org → 404; same-org
+  non-admins → 403.
+- `{uid}` must belong to `{orgID}` → otherwise 404. `toOrgId` must name an existing
+  organization (one that has at least one user or project) → otherwise 400. Moving a user
+  to the org they are already in → 409.
+- Project access does not move. The user's memberships in `{orgID}`'s projects are removed,
+  and tasks assigned to them in those projects are unassigned. This keeps the model rules
+  (members and assignees belong to the project's organization) true.
+- Org-admin rights are cleared, so they do not carry into the new organization.
+
 ## Seed data
 
 | User | Org | Roles |
